/-!
# Lifting étale algebra maps modulo a locally nilpotent ideal

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07K4, `lemma-smooth-strong-lift`, specialized to
étale algebras (blueprint: lem-sfb-etale-nil-ideal-map-lift).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Every algebra map from an étale algebra to a quotient by an elementwise nilpotent ideal
lifts to the original algebra. Zero rings are allowed, and the ideal need not have a uniform
nilpotence exponent.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 07K4, `lemma-smooth-strong-lift`, specialized to étale
algebras (blueprint: lem-sfb-etale-nil-ideal-map-lift).

Proof:
1. By `lem-weil-pbc-etale-ring-map-iff-etale-affine`, the affine étale hypothesis gives
   finite presentation, vanishing first cotangent homology and zero Kähler differentials.
   The last module is projective. By `def-weil-pbc-smooth-ring-map`, choose a presentation
   `C = A[x₁, …, xₙ]/(f₁, …, fₘ)` with finitely many generators and relations.
2. Lift the images under `g` of the polynomial generators to elements of `T`. Their
   relation errors `eⱼ` lie in `J`. The ideal `K` generated by these finitely many errors
   lies in `J`, and evaluation induces an algebra map `g₁ : C → T/K` reducing to `g`.
3. Choose positive exponents `dⱼ` with `eⱼ ^ dⱼ = 0` and set `M = 1 + ∑ⱼ (dⱼ - 1)`.
   Every monomial of degree `M` in the errors has some exponent at least `dⱼ`, hence
   vanishes. Thus `K ^ M = 0`. With no relations, `K = 0` and `M = 1`.
4. Inductively lift `g₁` to maps `gᵣ : C → T/K^r` for `1 ≤ r ≤ M`. The kernel of
   `T/K^(r+1) → T/K^r` is the image of `K^r`, whose square is zero since `2r ≥ r+1`.
   Its quotient is canonically `T/K^r`. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-smooth-ring-map-square-zero-lifting` with the cotangent hypotheses
   from step 1. Each lift continues to reduce to `g₁` modulo `K`.
5. Since `K ^ M = 0`, identify `T/K^M` with `T` to obtain `h`. Reducing first modulo
   `K` and then modulo `J` gives `g`, proving the required equality. If `M = 1`,
   this applies directly to `g₁`, with no induction successor step. -/
theorem exists_algHom_lift_of_etale_of_nil_ideal
    (A C : Type u) (T : Type v) [CommRing A] [CommRing C] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A C] [Algebra A T]
    (hEtale : Etale (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A C))))
    (J : Ideal T) (hJ : ∀ t : T, t ∈ J → ∃ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ t ^ n = 0)
    (g : C →ₐ[A] T ⧸ J) :
    ∃ h : C →ₐ[A] T, (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A J).comp h = g := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
